4.2 Amount. Any Sponsorship amount is sufficient to trigger the grant in
Section 4.1. The Licensor does not set a minimum. Any additional Sponsorship
amount supplied later is added to the existing licence.

4.3 Scope. A Sponsorship License is either a Business License or an
Individual License, determined under Section 5. The two differ only in who
may exercise the rights.

4.4 Duration. A Sponsorship License is perpetual and irrevocable with respect
to the versions of the Software published as of the date the Sponsorship is
received, and remains subject to Section 12. Ceasing to sponsor does not
terminate a Sponsorship License already granted, but does not extend it to
versions of the Software published afterward.


5. BUSINESS AND INDIVIDUAL LICENSES
===================================

5.1 Business License. A Sponsorship qualifies for a Business License only if
both of the following are true:

    (a) the Sponsorship is made from an email address at a domain controlled
        by the business, by a person authorized by that business to make
        purchases on its behalf; and

    (b) the sponsor identifies, at the time of the Sponsorship, the legal
        name of the business the license is for.

A Business License extends to the named business and its employees and
contractors, acting within the scope of that business.

5.2 Individual License. A Sponsorship made from a personal email address, or
that does not satisfy both conditions in Section 5.1, is an Individual
License.

An Individual License extends only to the natural person who made the
Sponsorship. It does not extend to that person's employer, client, or any
other entity, and it does not authorize Commercial Use on behalf of any such
entity. It authorizes Commercial Use only by that person, for that person's
own account.

5.3 No implied upgrade. A Sponsorship from a personal email address does not
become a Business License because the sponsor is employed by a business, is
reimbursed by a business, or uses the Software at a business. A business
seeking a Business License must sponsor in accordance with Section 5.1.

5.4 Correction. If a Sponsorship intended as a Business License was made in a
way that does not satisfy Section 5.1, the sponsor may contact the Licensor to
have it reclassified. The Licensor may, but is not obliged to, reclassify it.


